Hey Vishnu — I took your LangSmith integration and adapted it for the direct-Chinou BSM build. I kept the Runs API foundation you put together, but made a few changes mainly around latency and getting accurate metrics through.

The biggest one is the Sync slowdown. Your version was making three synchronous calls per email on the extraction path, which was adding roughly 2× latency. We now buffer the full trace and send it in a single **POST /runs/batch** via **executeAsync**, so there’s basically no added latency.

A few other updates:

* The child run now reports Chinou’s actual `execution_time_ms` instead of showing 0 ms.
* We’re passing through Chinou’s real `cost_usd` as well.
* Tokens still fall back to the same char/4 estimate since Chinou returns empty counts during eval, but it’ll automatically use the real token counts once `ChinouClient` exposes them.
* I also added a kill switch, sampling, proper error runs so failures show up red, and a `ping()` self-test.

So overall, it’s still built on your Runs API approach — just tuned for the direct-Chinou path and wired up with the actual latency/cost data.
